{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q012_not_true_family_specific_pair","answer":"Yes, at the level SCOPe uses, but this is a weak, formal kind of homology. In SCOPe 2.08, d1s9za_ (1s9z A:, Protein "Amyloidogenic design-1", sunid 103785) and d1hqja_ (1hqj A:, Protein "Unnamed design-1", sunid 100906) are in the same Family. That family is k.40.1.1, "Designed trimeric coiled-coil" (sunid 100905). They also share the superfamily k.40.1 (sunid 100904), the fold k.40 (sunid 100903), and the class k (sunid 58788, "Designed proteins"). They sit in different Protein nodes, and each has its own "Synthetic" species node (103786 and 64668). The shared family is therefore the lowest shared level, and SCOPe's hierarchy implies homology between the two domains.

The caveats are important. Neither domain is a natural protein, so "homologous" here does not mean common descent from a shared natural ancestor. Both are de novo designed trimeric coiled-coil peptides grouped by shared design and structure. SCOPe class k holds designed proteins, and the family placement reflects the same designed architecture. It is not evidence of evolutionary divergence. The two entries are different designs (the names differ), so being in the same family does not make them the same protein or give them the same sequence. I did not compare their sequences. The shared family also does not establish equivalent function, stability, amyloidogenic behavior, ligand binding, or interchangeable use as templates. The "Amyloidogenic design-1" and "Unnamed design-1" names are only Protein-level labels.

The annotation and homology responses for both domains show no inconsistencies, repeats, heterogeneity, or homology warnings. The only comments are ligand/ion notes: 1s9z is "complexed with na, zn" and 1hqj is "complexed with pb, sin, so4". These are not evidence of function. The absence of warnings does not add positive evidence. I did not retrieve BLAST or FATCAT hits, because the question asks only about SCOPe classification, and I did not check the older releases.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","mcp__scope__compare_scop_domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1s9za_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1hqja_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1s9za_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1hqja_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1s9za_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1hqja_/homology"]}]}
